history|Who was the first president of the United States?|George Washington.
history|Who wrote the Declaration of Independence?|Thomas Jefferson was its main writer.
history|In what year did the United States declare independence?|1776.
history|Who built the pyramids of Giza?|Ancient Egyptians.
history|What were the ancient Olympic Games?|Sports festivals held in ancient Greece.
history|Who invented the light bulb that became popular?|Thomas Edison made the first practical one.
history|Who invented the telephone?|Alexander Graham Bell is credited with it.
history|Who were the Wright brothers?|The first people to fly a powered airplane, in 1903.
history|Who painted the Mona Lisa?|Leonardo da Vinci.
history|Who was Martin Luther King Jr.?|A leader who fought for civil rights and equality with peace.
history|Who was Abraham Lincoln?|The 16th president of the United States.
history|What was the Great Wall of China built for?|To protect against invaders.
history|Who was Cleopatra?|A queen of ancient Egypt.
history|What were dinosaurs?|Ancient reptiles that lived millions of years ago.
history|When did the dinosaurs die out?|About 66 million years ago.
history|What is the Stone Age?|A very early time when people made tools from stone.
history|Who was Albert Einstein?|A scientist famous for the theory of relativity.
history|Who was Marie Curie?|A scientist who studied radioactivity and won two Nobel Prizes.
history|Who was Isaac Newton?|A scientist who described gravity and motion.
history|Who was Galileo?|An astronomer who studied the sky with a telescope.
history|What was the printing press?|A machine that printed books, made popular by Gutenberg.
history|Who was Rosa Parks?|A woman who bravely refused to give up her bus seat.
history|Who were the Vikings?|Seafaring people from Scandinavia long ago.
history|What did the Romans build to carry water?|Aqueducts.
history|Who sailed across the Atlantic in 1492?|Christopher Columbus.
history|What was the first animal sent into orbit?|A dog named Laika.
history|What year did people first land on the Moon?|1969.
history|Who was Mozart?|A famous composer from Austria.
history|Who was Beethoven?|A German composer who kept writing music even after losing his hearing.
history|Who was Harriet Tubman?|A brave woman who led many people to freedom.
health|Why should we wash our hands?|To wash away germs.
health|How much sleep do kids need?|About 9 to 12 hours a night.
health|Why is water good for you?|Your body needs it to work and stay cool.
health|Why do we exercise?|It keeps your heart, muscles and mood strong.
health|What do vegetables give us?|Vitamins, minerals and fiber.
health|What does the heart do?|It pumps blood around your body.
health|What do lungs do?|They breathe in air and take oxygen into your blood.
health|What does the brain do?|It thinks, feels and controls your body.
health|What do bones do?|They hold you up and protect your organs.
health|What do muscles do?|They help you move.
health|What does the stomach do?|It helps break down food.
health|Why do we sneeze?|To blow out something bugging your nose.
health|Why do we yawn?|Often when we are tired, but scientists are still curious why.
health|What gives us energy?|Food and rest.
health|What vitamin do we get from sunshine?|Vitamin D.
health|Why do we cover our mouth when we cough?|So germs don't spread to others.
health|What helps a small cut heal?|Cleaning it and covering it with a bandage.
health|How many teeth do adults usually have?|32.
health|How many baby teeth do kids have?|20.
health|What are the five senses?|Sight, hearing, smell, taste and touch.
how|How does a rainbow form?|Sunlight bends and splits inside raindrops.
how|How do airplanes fly?|Their wings push air down and create lift.
how|How does a fridge keep food cold?|It pumps heat out from inside.
how|How do plants make food?|Photosynthesis, using sunlight, water and air.
how|How does a magnet work?|Its tiny parts line up and pull on iron.
how|How do boats float?|They push aside enough water to hold them up.
how|How does a light bulb glow?|Electricity heats or excites it until it gives off light.
how|How do clouds form?|Water vapor cools into tiny droplets.
how|Why does it rain?|Cloud droplets join until they are heavy enough to fall.
how|What causes thunder?|Lightning heats the air so fast it booms.
how|What causes the seasons?|Earth's tilt as it goes around the Sun.
how|Why does the Moon change shape?|We see different parts of its sunlit side.
how|What causes tides?|Mostly the Moon's gravity.
how|How does a phone call work?|Your voice turns into signals that travel to the other phone.
how|What is electricity?|Moving tiny charged particles called electrons.
how|How do bees make honey?|They collect nectar and dry it in the hive.
how|How does ice melt?|It warms up above zero degrees Celsius.
how|How does a seed grow?|With water, warmth and light it sprouts roots and a shoot.
how|How do birds fly?|They flap wings that push air down.
how|What makes wind?|Air moving from high pressure to low pressure.
how|How does a compass work?|Its needle points to Earth's magnetic north.
how|How does soap clean?|It grabs grease and lets water wash it away.
how|What is the internet?|Lots of computers connected so they can share information.
how|How does a volcano erupt?|Melted rock pushes up and bursts out.
how|What makes an earthquake?|Big pieces of Earth's crust slipping.
how|How do we hear sounds?|Sound waves wiggle our eardrums.
how|How do we see?|Light enters our eyes and our brain makes a picture.
how|Why do leaves change color in autumn?|Green chlorophyll fades and other colors show.
how|How does a bicycle move?|Pedals turn a chain that turns the back wheel.
how|What does a battery do?|It stores energy as chemicals and gives it out as electricity.
science|What is gravity?|A force that pulls things toward each other.
science|What is an atom?|A tiny building block of everything.
science|What is a molecule?|Atoms joined together.
science|What is DNA?|The instructions inside living cells.
science|What is a cell?|The smallest living unit of life.
science|What is energy?|The ability to make things move or change.
science|What is friction?|A force that slows things rubbing together.
science|What is evaporation?|Liquid turning into gas.
science|What is condensation?|Gas turning into liquid.
science|What is the speed of light?|About 300,000 kilometers per second.
science|What is sound?|Vibrations traveling through air or other stuff.
science|What is a solar panel?|A panel that turns sunlight into electricity.
science|What is a habitat?|The natural home of a plant or animal.
science|What is a food chain?|Who eats whom in nature.
science|What is erosion?|Wind or water slowly wearing land away.
science|What are the layers of the Earth?|Crust, mantle, outer core and inner core.
science|What is lava called underground?|Magma.
science|What is a mammal?|A warm-blooded animal with hair that feeds its babies milk.
science|What is a reptile?|A cold-blooded animal with scales.
science|What is an amphibian?|An animal that lives in water and on land, like a frog.
science|What is a skeleton?|The frame of bones inside a body.
science|What is pollination?|Moving pollen so flowers make seeds.
science|What is a thermometer for?|Measuring temperature.
science|What is a microscope for?|Seeing very tiny things.
science|What is a telescope for?|Seeing faraway things like stars.
science|What is the boiling point of water in Fahrenheit?|212 degrees.
science|What is the freezing point of water in Fahrenheit?|32 degrees.
science|What is steam?|Water as a gas.
science|What is a liquid?|Something that flows and takes the shape of its container.
science|What are germs?|Tiny living things that can make us sick.
space|What is the Sun made of?|Mostly hydrogen and helium.
space|How far is the Sun from Earth?|About 150 million kilometers.
space|How long does sunlight take to reach Earth?|About 8 minutes.
space|What is a comet?|A ball of ice and dust with a glowing tail.
space|What is an asteroid?|A rocky object orbiting the Sun.
space|What is a constellation?|A pattern of stars in the sky.
space|What is the Big Dipper?|A star pattern shaped like a ladle.
space|What is the North Star called?|Polaris.
space|What is an astronaut?|A person trained to travel in space.
space|What is the International Space Station?|A big lab orbiting Earth where astronauts live.
space|What is a light-year?|The distance light travels in one year.
space|What is a supernova?|A giant star exploding.
space|What is a nebula?|A cloud of gas and dust where stars can be born.
space|Why do stars twinkle?|Earth's moving air bends their light.
space|What is a moon?|A natural object that orbits a planet.
space|Is there air on the Moon?|No.
space|What is an orbit?|The path one object takes around another.
space|What is the Milky Way?|Our home galaxy.
space|What is the closest galaxy like ours?|Andromeda.
space|What is a dwarf planet?|A small round world like Pluto.
space|Is Pluto a planet?|It is called a dwarf planet now.
space|What is a solar eclipse?|The Moon blocking the Sun.
space|What is a lunar eclipse?|Earth's shadow covering the Moon.
space|What is a rocket?|A vehicle that pushes out hot gas to fly into space.
space|How old is the universe?|About 13.8 billion years.
space|How old is Earth?|About 4.5 billion years.
art|What are the primary colors in painting?|Red, yellow and blue.
art|What is a sculpture?|Art shaped in three dimensions, like clay or stone.
art|What is a portrait?|A picture of a person.
art|What is a landscape painting?|A picture of nature or scenery.
art|What do artists use to paint?|Brushes and paint.
art|What is a sketch?|A quick rough drawing.
art|Who painted The Starry Night?|Vincent van Gogh.
art|What is a mosaic?|A picture made from small colored pieces.
art|What is origami?|The art of folding paper.
art|What is pixel art?|Pictures made from tiny squares, like old games.
art|What is animation?|Many pictures shown fast so they seem to move.
art|What are warm colors?|Red, orange and yellow.
art|What are cool colors?|Blue, green and purple.
art|What is a sprite in games?|A small picture of a character or object.
music|What is a melody?|The tune you can hum.
music|What is harmony?|Different notes sounding together nicely.
music|What is tempo?|How fast or slow music goes.
music|What does BPM mean?|Beats per minute.
music|What is a chord?|Three or more notes played together.
music|What is an orchestra?|A big group of musicians playing together.
music|What is a conductor?|The person who leads an orchestra.
music|What is a duet?|Music for two performers.
music|What is a solo?|Music performed by one person.
music|How many keys does a full piano have?|88.
music|What is a major key?|A key that usually sounds bright and happy.
music|What is a minor key?|A key that often sounds moodier or sadder.
music|What is a beat?|The steady pulse of music.
music|What is a lyric?|The words of a song.
music|What is an echo?|A sound bouncing back to you.
kind|What can you say to cheer someone up?|You're doing great, and I'm here for you.
kind|What is empathy?|Understanding how someone else feels.
kind|What is gratitude?|Feeling thankful.
kind|What is patience?|Waiting calmly.
kind|What is courage?|Doing something even when you feel scared.
kind|What is honesty?|Telling the truth.
kind|How can you be a good friend?|Listen, share and be kind.
kind|What should you do if someone is left out?|Invite them to join.
kind|How do you calm down?|Breathe slowly and count to five.
kind|Is it okay to cry?|Yes, crying helps let feelings out.
kind|What do you say when you're wrong?|I'm sorry, I'll do better.
kind|What makes a good apology?|Saying sorry, meaning it and making it right.
kind|What does it mean to forgive?|Letting go of being upset with someone.
kind|How do you show love?|Kind words, hugs, time and help.
kind|What does respect mean?|Treating people like they matter.
kind|What can you do when a friend is happy?|Be happy with them.
kind|How can you help at home?|Clean up and lend a hand.
kind|What helps when you feel nervous?|Deep breaths and remembering you can do it.
kind|What is a compliment?|Something nice you say about someone.
kind|Why is sharing nice?|It makes others feel cared for.
nature|What is the biggest tree?|The giant sequoia by volume.
nature|What is the tallest tree?|The coast redwood.
nature|What is a desert?|A place that gets very little rain.
nature|What is a rainforest?|A thick forest with lots of rain.
nature|What is a coral reef?|An underwater home built by tiny animals called corals.
nature|What is a volcano?|A mountain that can erupt with lava.
nature|What is a glacier?|A huge slow river of ice.
nature|What is an island?|Land with water all around it.
nature|What is a canyon?|A deep valley carved by a river.
nature|What is a waterfall?|Water falling over a cliff.
nature|What are the four seasons?|Spring, summer, autumn and winter.
nature|What is a hurricane?|A huge spinning storm over warm ocean.
nature|What is a tornado?|A spinning column of wind.
nature|What is snow?|Frozen water crystals falling from clouds.
nature|What is fog?|A cloud near the ground.
nature|What do roots do?|Hold plants in the ground and drink water.
nature|What do flowers make?|Seeds.
nature|What is moss?|A small soft plant that grows in damp places.
nature|What is a mushroom?|A fungus, not a plant.
nature|Do all birds fly?|No, penguins and ostriches can't.
nature|What is the biggest bird?|The ostrich.
nature|What is the smallest bird?|The bee hummingbird.
nature|What animal has the longest neck?|The giraffe.
nature|How do fish breathe?|With gills.
nature|What do bees help plants do?|Make seeds by spreading pollen.
nature|What is hibernation?|A long deep sleep through winter.
nature|What is migration?|Animals traveling far when seasons change.
nature|What is camouflage?|Colors that help animals hide.
nature|Which animal is known for changing colors?|The chameleon.
nature|What do worms do for soil?|They mix it and make it healthier.
nature|What is the biggest cat?|The tiger.
nature|What is the slowest mammal?|The sloth.
nature|What animal sleeps hanging upside down?|Bats.
nature|What is an octopus known for?|Eight arms and being super smart.
nature|How many hearts does an octopus have?|Three.
geo|What is the biggest country by area?|Russia.
geo|What country has the most people?|India.
geo|What is the smallest country?|Vatican City.
geo|What is the equator?|An imaginary line around the middle of Earth.
geo|What is a map?|A drawing of a place from above.
geo|What are the seven continents?|Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia, Europe, North America and South America.
geo|What are the five oceans?|Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern and Arctic.
geo|Which ocean is the biggest?|The Pacific.
geo|Which continent is the coldest?|Antarctica.
geo|What is the largest hot desert?|The Sahara.
geo|What is the largest rainforest?|The Amazon.
geo|What is the longest river in the United States?|The Missouri River.
geo|Where is the Eiffel Tower?|In Paris, France.
geo|Where is the Statue of Liberty?|In New York Harbor.
geo|Where are the pyramids of Giza?|In Egypt.
geo|Where is Mount Everest?|On the border of Nepal and China.
geo|What is the North Pole?|The northernmost point of Earth.
geo|Where do kangaroos live in the wild?|Australia.
geo|Where do polar bears live?|The Arctic.
geo|Where do penguins live in the wild?|Mostly the Southern Hemisphere.
geo|What is a peninsula?|Land with water on three sides.
geo|What state is Chicago in?|Illinois.
geo|What is the biggest US state?|Alaska.
geo|What is the smallest US state?|Rhode Island.
geo|How many US states are there?|Fifty.
